  stagingMessage: 'The six ground-lit boosters burn out and drop away.

    The three
    air-lit boosters ignite!'
  cruiseMessage: 'Opportunity is on its way to Mars!

    Landing: Meridiani Planum,
    January 25, 2004 UTC (January 24 local time).


    (Real launch timeline sped
    up.)'
  briefingNarrationText: NASA's Mars Exploration Rover-B, Opportunity, launched aboard
    a Delta II 7925H from Cape Canaveral Air Force Station on July 7, 2003, at 11:18
    p.m. Eastern Daylight Time. Its mission was to investigate evidence of past water
    on Mars. Press the red launch button when you are ready. This is a shortened
    educational reenactment.
  countdownNarrationText:
  internalPowerNarrationText: Launch vehicle on internal power.
  ignitionNarrationText: Main engine start!
  liftoffNarrationText: 'LIFTOFF!

    Delta II lifts off carrying the Opportunity
    rover to Mars.'
  pitchNarrationText: 'Pitching over and heading east, out over the Atlantic Ocean.

    Six
    ground-lit GEM-46 boosters at full thrust.'
  stagingNarrationText: 'The six ground-lit boosters burn out and drop away.

    The
    three air-lit boosters ignite!'
  cruiseNarrationText: 'Opportunity is on its way to Mars!

    Landing: Meridiani
    Planum, January 25, 2004 UTC (January 24 local time).


    (Real launch timeline
    sped up.)'
